Omission
- [N1] Omitted trace (input 0): i1:To start the process, begin by supplying the requirement and then documenting it. -> i2:If the order is received via fax, input the order into an Excel file. -> i4:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. -> i5:Upon receiving the Excel list, type the orders into the MS-Access database. -> i6:After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. -> i7:Once the database is completed, control the incoming order. At the same time, continue to do the check. -> i8:If the order is correct, release it. -> i9:Send the Excel list to the student and upon receiving it, continue with the process. -> i11:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. -> i14:Once the order is signed off, contact the client and release the order. -> i15:Once the order is received by PPC, they will initiate production. -> i16:If the issue cannot be solved, cancel the order. -> i19:If the order needs to be cancelled, the process ends.
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:To start the process, begin by supplying the requirement and then documenting it. -> i2:If the order is received via fax, input the order into an Excel file. -> i4:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. -> i5:Upon receiving the Excel list, type the orders into the MS-Access database. -> i6:After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. -> i7:Once the database is completed, control the incoming order. At the same time, continue to do the check. -> i8:If the order is correct, release it. -> i9:Send the Excel list to the student and upon receiving it, continue with the process. -> i11:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. -> i14:Once the order is signed off, contact the client and release the order. -> i15:Once the order is received by PPC, they will initiate production. -> i17:If the issue can be solved, release the order. -> i18:After PPC initiates production, the goods will be produced. -> i20:If not, check the quality of the goods. -> i21:Once the quality is checked, create and send a quality report to the finance department. -> i22:Release the order via memo and ensure that the memo is achieved in the warehouse. -> i23:Send the invoice and once it is sent, report the achievement to the finance department. -> i26:Finally, archive the memo and close the order. This marks the end of the process.
